    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26pM3Zm2FmiHEQC3LdDGD9g)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent of other open PRs; touches only `sp-org-lint-footnotes.el`, its literate doc `sp-org-lint.org` and `tests/sp-org-lint-test.el`.\n- Based on current `main`, which already has #470 merged.\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-io5kcr`, not number-prefixed: a cloud session cannot rename its branch once the PR number is known.\n\n## What and why\n\n- `M-x sp-org-lint-footnotes` failed with `Cannot open load file: sp-interaction`.\n- Cause:\n  - The worker is a bare `emacs -Q --batch` with only `funct/` on its `-L` path.\n  - Since the echo-area hints work, `sp-batch-report` requires `sp-interaction`, which is in `base/`.\n- Fix, in `sp-org-lint.org` (tangled to `sp-org-lint-footnotes.el`):\n  - `sp-org-lint-fn--worker-load-dirs`: the library folder, its parent and the parent's sub-folders, like the recursive load path of `init.el`.\n  - `sp-org-lint-fn--worker-command`: builds the command line (testable); `sp-org-lint-fn--start` uses it.\n- Two more breakages sat behind the first one, now fixed:\n  - With `base/` on the path the worker would have loaded `sp-globals`, which needs `early-init.el` (`sp-cache-dir` void). The worker sets `sp-org-lint-fn--worker` and skips it.\n  - `sp-org-lint-fn-backup-directory` used `sp-var-dir` at load time, void in a bare Emacs. It now falls back to `user-emacs-directory`.\n- Other workers: it is the only place that spawns `emacs` (`invocation-name`); the other batch commands run in-process via `sp-async-work`.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New ERT tests in `sp-org-lint-test.el`:\n  - the worker command, run for real in a bare Emacs (`EMACSLOADPATH` empty), exits 0 and prints `(:done t)`\n  - the worker load path contains `sp-interaction.el` and `sp-batch-report.el`\n- `sp-org-lint-test.el`: 17/17 pass, Emacs 29.3 batch. Before the fix, the old worker command fails with the exact error above.\n- `tools/check-tangle.sh` passes.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Real vault, real `vulpea-db-query`, GUI Emacs 31, macOS (Homebrew Emacs path in `invocation-directory`).\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [x] `M-x sp-org-lint-footnotes` on the real vault: the scan runs and the report opens, no \"worker Emacs failed\"\n- [x] `a` in the report applies the moves; a backup copy is written\n- [x] `*sp-org-lint footnotes*` hints in the echo area still show\n- [ ] `emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/funct -L libraries/modules/base -l tests/sp-org-lint-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` passes (needs the `sp-var-dir` constants from `early-init.el`)\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiD22hb7nU9mVzT6YQk)_",
